CAPL basics
code is divided into sections,
sections start with console argument,
where "none" is reserved for blank argument,
and other arguments need to start with "-",
as non "-" args are inputs.
Each block ends with designated EO.

Basic "Hello world"

null
	write
		Hello world!
	endwrite
EOA
EOF

As seen above, both EOA and EOF is used,
althought, EOF is optional, EOA needs to
be used.

Block closing operators

EOA - closes argument
EOF - closes file
endwrite - stops output session
endfile - stops file involving session
endif - closes if

IO commands

write - endwrite
	writes lines of blank text to terminal.

readfile, writefile, openfile - endfile
	readfile - reads whole file and outputs
	it to a terminal as a text
	writefile - writes particular line to file
	openfile - opens file as current data stream
	to read particular line or segment, or write
	to particular line using "writefileline"

LOGIC operators

if then - endif
	looks at bool value, or int if true, or higher than 0,
	executes itself, execution starts from "then" statment, 
	which can be allocated anywhere after if.

then loop
	in combination with if can create loop which will
	check validity after every iteration


